DESCRIPTION:Name of Event: &nbsp\;Story &amp\; Verse: A Storytelling and P
 oetic Open Mic Date: &nbsp\;October 22\, 2026 Start/End Time: &nbsp\;7:00 
 pm - 9:00 pm Address: &nbsp\;102 Witherspoon Street\, Princeton\, NJ 08542
  Theme: &nbsp\;From Dusk Till Dawn Host: &nbsp\;Brass Rabbit Price: &nbsp\
 ;FREE Phone: &nbsp\; (609) 924-8777 Email Address: &nbsp\; fclark@artscoun
 cilofprinceton.org Website: &nbsp\; http://artscouncilofprinceton.org/even
 t/story-verse-a-storytelling-and-poetic-open-mic-oct26/ Social Media: &nbs
 p\; @artscouncilofprinceton Event Description: &nbsp\;Share your story\, y
 our poetry\, or your prose\, based on the monthly theme! Story &amp\; Vers
 e provides a warm and welcoming spotlight for both emerging and establishe
 d artists in our Solley Theater\, an intimate space in the heart of Downto
 wn Princeton. Join us as a performer: Prepare a story\, poem\, or spoken w
 ord piece up to 5 minutes in length and (at least loosely) related to the 
 theme. This month’s theme is “From Dusk Till Dawn“ Arrive by 6:45pm 
 to add your name to the hat. No previous experience or pre-registration ne
 cessary. Join our audience: Take the elevator or stairs to the Solley Thea
 ter\, located on the top floor of our Paul Robeson Center for the Arts. Op
 tional: participate from your seat with a Micro Story. Read the printed pr
 ompt based on the evening’s theme and respond with a super concise story
  (just a line or two!) that answers the question. Brass Rabbit will read y
 our story at the mic\, as time allows. Find a seat and enjoy the performan
 ces. We kick off shortly after 7pm.
LOCATION:102 Witherspoon Lane\, Princeton\, NJ\, 08542
