DESCRIPTION:Name of Event: &nbsp\;Story &amp\; Verse: A Storytelling and P
 oetic Open Mic Date: &nbsp\;November 19\, 2026 Start/End Time: &nbsp\;7:00
  pm - 9:00 pm Address: &nbsp\;102 Witherspoon Street\, Princeton\, NJ 0854
 2 Theme: &nbsp\;Open Theme Host: &nbsp\;Brass Rabbit Price: &nbsp\;FREE Ph
 one: &nbsp\; (609) 924-8777 Email Address: &nbsp\; fclark@artscouncilofpri
 nceton.org Website: &nbsp\; http://artscouncilofprinceton.org/event/story-
 verse-a-storytelling-and-poetic-open-mic-oct26/ Social Media: &nbsp\; @art
 scouncilofprinceton Event Description: &nbsp\;Share your story\, your poet
 ry\, or your prose\, based on the monthly theme! Story &amp\; Verse provid
 es a warm and welcoming spotlight for both emerging and established artist
 s in our Solley Theater\, an intimate space in the heart of Downtown Princ
 eton. Join us as a performer: Prepare a story\, poem\, or spoken word piec
 e up to 5 minutes in length and (at least loosely) related to the theme. T
 his month’s theme is open\, so share whatever you feel inspired to. Arri
 ve by 6:45pm to add your name to the hat. No previous experience or pre-re
 gistration necessary. Join our audience: Take the elevator or stairs to th
 e Solley Theater\, located on the top floor of our Paul Robeson Center for
  the Arts. Optional: participate from your seat with a Micro Story. Read t
 he printed prompt based on the evening’s theme and respond with a super 
 concise story (just a line or two!) that answers the question. Brass Rabbi
 t will read your story at the mic\, as time allows. Find a seat and enjoy 
 the performances. We kick off shortly after 7pm.
LOCATION:102 Witherspoon Lane\, Princeton\, NJ\, 08542
