DESCRIPTION:It's time to LET FRESH FIRE FALL!&nbsp\; The final night of a 
 three month residency is &nbsp\; Friday December 11 2026&nbsp\;@ 7:00PM .&
 nbsp\; 601 Doctor Martin Luther King Junior Boulevard Basement\, Newark\, 
 NJ 07102 Let Fresh Fire Fall is a Faith Based Open Mic that highlights Chr
 istian Poets.&nbsp\; Many thanks to&nbsp\;Mayowa Okubanjo (GODSENT) for th
 e&nbsp\;opportunity! &nbsp\; Tickets&nbsp\;are $15 and can be purchased on
 line here: LetFreshFireDec11.eventbrite.com NO TICKETS SOLD AT THE DOOR .&
 nbsp\; Featuring for December 11 :&nbsp\; CrimZon Red &amp\; The Poetic i2
 i Event is open to all poets regardless of religious background or none at
  all.&nbsp\; You'll hear poetry from people of all backgrounds with underl
 ying messages of&nbsp\; faith\, hope\, love\, perseverance\, healing\, del
 iverance\, and joy among other topics.&nbsp\; Our aim is to glorify God an
 d be an inspiration and a light in the darkness. &nbsp\; Come with an open
  mind and heart to see and hear how Christian Poets bring the poetic fire!
 &nbsp\; Poetry containing any profanity or explicit content will NOT be al
 lowed . &nbsp\; The Open&nbsp\;Mic list is limited to ten (10) spots so co
 me early to secure your spot.&nbsp\; One (1) poem per person on the open m
 ic list. &nbsp\; If time permits\, any poets&nbsp\; on the Open Mic list&n
 bsp\;that wants to read another poem can. If you're interested in being a 
 vendor\, please call&nbsp\; (646) 372-6230 &nbsp\; or email&nbsp\; PoetsWi
 thPurpose@gmail.com .&nbsp\; I look forward to seeing you there!&nbsp\; TH
